  "id": "situational-conditions",
  "term": "situational conditions",
  "definition": "Situational conditions are features of a particular context that shape how people can act and how strongly an intervention affects behavior. In this source, they refer to contextual factors such as the lower autonomy available at work compared with home, which can limit behavior change.",
